            <ArticleTitle>ColorSketch: A Drawing Assistant for Generating Color Sketches from Photos.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>70-81</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1109/MCG.2016.37</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A color sketch creates a vivid depiction of a scene using sparse pencil strokes and casual colored brush strokes. The interactive drawing system ColorSketch can help novice users generate color sketches from photos. To preserve artistic freedom and expressiveness, the proposed system gives users full control over pencil strokes, while automatically augmenting pencil sketches using color mapping, brush stroke rendering, and blank area creation. Experimental and user study results demonstrate that users, especially novices, can create better color sketches with our system than when using traditional manual tools.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
